5. SUB-PRODUCT IDENTIFICATION & POPULATION RULES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CRITICAL FILTERING — TWO-GATE TEST:
A clause is ONLY extracted as a Sub-Product if it passes BOTH gates:

GATE 1 — MUST contain at least one of these keywords (or direct synonyms):
  System Administrator(s), online banking profile, subscribe for electronic banking,
  electronic banking services, internet banking services, electronic platforms,
  E-banking, HSBCnet, H2H, API's, Channels (in a digital context), authorisation levels
  (on a digital platform), third parties to manage Channels.

GATE 2 — MUST NOT be a general banking power.
  Reject any clause whose PRIMARY action is opening/closing accounts, general delegation
  of authority, provision of general banking services, or execution of general documents —
  UNLESS the clause explicitly and directly ties that action to electronic platforms or Channels.

Step 1 — Link qualifying sub-products to each Account Number from Section 4.
Step 2 — Each qualifying sub-product gets its own object in the "Sub-Products" array
          with its own "Signing Rule" array.
If no clauses pass both gates, set "Sub-Products": []
